IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `itaa-super`

-- Income Tax Assessment Act 1997, ss 290-230, 290-235, 292-85, 292-102, 294-30, 294-35, 301-10, 302-60, 302-145, 302-195 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_income-tax-assessment-act-1997_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

`Chloe's downsizer contribution (c094)` MEANS Downsizer WITH
    `age when contributing` IS 67
    `main residence exemption applied at least partly` IS TRUE
    `years held by the couple before the disposal` IS 30
    `dwelling in Australia and not mobile` IS TRUE
    `days after the change of ownership` IS 30
    `Commissioner allowed longer` IS FALSE
    `chosen` IS TRUE
    `earlier downsizer from another dwelling` IS FALSE
    `amount contributed` IS 300000
    `your earlier downsizer contributions` IS 0
    `capital proceeds of both interests` IS 1500000
    `other downsizer contributions from these proceeds` IS 0

`Liam's downsizer contribution (c094)` MEANS Downsizer WITH
    `age when contributing` IS 70
    `main residence exemption applied at least partly` IS TRUE
    `years held by the couple before the disposal` IS 30
    `dwelling in Australia and not mobile` IS TRUE
    `days after the change of ownership` IS 30
    `Commissioner allowed longer` IS FALSE
    `chosen` IS TRUE
    `earlier downsizer from another dwelling` IS FALSE
    `amount contributed` IS 300000
    `your earlier downsizer contributions` IS 0
    `capital proceeds of both interests` IS 1500000
    `other downsizer contributions from these proceeds` IS 300000

§ `ss 290-230, 290-235`

-- c057: Chloe contributes $3,000 for Liam's low-income year (his income is not stated; hypothetical 30,000): 18% of 3,000 = 540.
-- At 40,000 (not less than $40,000): nil.
#ASSERT `What spouse contribution offset do I get` 30000 3000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS 540
#ASSERT `What spouse contribution offset do I get` 40000 3000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS 0

§ `s 292-85(2)`

-- k089: Jake's $100,000. At the 2017-18 concessional cap of $25,000 the cap is 4 x 25,000 = 100,000; nil once the total
-- balance has reached the general transfer balance cap.
#ASSERT `What is my non-concessional cap` 25000 500000 2000000 EQUALS 100000
#ASSERT `What is my non-concessional cap` 30000 2000000 2000000 EQUALS 0

§ `s 292-102`

-- c094: $300,000 each from Baldivis (held 30 years; proceeds hypothetical 1,500,000).
#ASSERT `How much is my downsizer contribution` `Chloe's downsizer contribution (c094)` EQUALS 300000
#ASSERT `How much is my downsizer contribution` `Liam's downsizer contribution (c094)` EQUALS 300000

§ `ss 294-30, 294-35`

-- d083: Daniel starts his account-based pension in 2063; the cap for that year is an indexed figure passed in. For a first
-- pension in 2017-18 the Act fixes $1,600,000. Credits of 1,700,000 against that cap: an excess of 100,000.
#ASSERT `What is my transfer balance cap` 2017 0 EQUALS 1600000

#ASSERT `What is my excess transfer balance` 1700000 0 1600000 EQUALS 100000

§ `ss 301-10 to 301-40`

-- c092: Chloe's pension at 63, and d083: Daniel's at 67 -- nothing assessable. Under 60 the taxable component is.
#ASSERT `How much of my super benefit is assessable` 63 400000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How much of my super benefit is assessable` 67 400000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How much of my super benefit is assessable` 58 400000 EQUALS 400000

§ `ss 302-60, 302-140, 302-145, 302-195`

-- c087 (the super to Sue, his widow), c096 (Liam's to Chloe), d093 (Daniel's to Priya): a spouse is a dependant; nothing
-- assessable. c098 (Chloe's to Oliver 58 and Ella 55) and k098 (Jake's to Ruby, 46): an adult child is not, unless dependent or
-- interdependent; the taxable component (hypothetical 300,000) is assessable, at no more than 15% on the element taxed in the fund.
#ASSERT `Am I a death benefits dependant` `the spouse or former spouse` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Am I a death benefits dependant` `an adult child` FALSE

#ASSERT `How much of the death benefit is assessable to me` `the spouse or former spouse` FALSE 300000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How much of the death benefit is assessable to me` `an adult child` FALSE 300000 EQUALS 300000

#ASSERT `What is the most I can be taxed on the death benefit in percent` FALSE EQUALS 15

